      "content": "For the two-stage cooling process, the temperature requirements are as follows: \n\n- Within two hours of cooking, the cooled poultry must reach 70°F (21°C) or below.\n- Within 4 to 6 hours of cooking, the cooled poultry must reach 40°F (4°C) or below.\n- At no point between cooling stages can the poultry enter the 'danger zone' of 40°F (4°C) to 140°F (60°C), as Clostridium perfringens can continue to grow during this period.",
